## 1. About BeLikeLocal and these terms

BeLikeLocal ("the platform", "we", "us") is operated by {{operator_name}}, {{operator_address}}, {{operator_registration}}. These terms apply to everyone who uses the platform: travellers who are looking for a guide ("travellers" or "visitors") and guides who offer their services ("guides").

By creating an account you accept these terms and confirm that you are at least 18 years old, or the age of majority where you live if that is higher. Travellers also accept the Traveller Agreement and guides the Guide Agreement; they add to these terms, and these terms prevail if they conflict.

## 2. What the platform does

BeLikeLocal is a meeting place. It helps travellers and guides find each other, show mutual interest, talk through the platform''s chat and book a meeting. Any tour, activity or other service is agreed directly between the traveller and the guide. We are not a party to that agreement. We do not employ guides or act as their agent, and we do not organise, supervise or check the services they provide.

### 2.1 Accounts and roles

One account can be a traveller, a guide or both. You choose the role you start with and can add the other later by accepting its agreement. You act in one role at a time; your profile text, interests, matches, bookings, reviews and level are kept separately for each role.

### 2.2 Finding each other

Travellers browse guides and guides browse travellers, one profile at a time, and choose "Interested" or "Reject". Profiles are ordered by an automatic ranking that takes into account how close the person is to the place you search, their reviews, their level, whether their identity has been verified, whether their profile is complete and how new their account is. Badges show the facts behind it (verified, top rated, trips completed, level). Nobody can pay for a better place.

You can search near a place: a guide sets the area where they guide and how far they travel; a traveller can set where they are looking, which guides see as the town only. Travellers can also plan a trip with several stops; the planner suggests guides for each stop with the help of an AI service (section 9.9), and guides see the town and dates of a traveller''s upcoming stops, never more.

### 2.3 Picks, matches and chat

A traveller shows interest using a pick from a selection pack (section 5.2). When both sides are interested, it is a match. Matched people can write to each other and share a location in the chat. Contact details are never shared: the platform automatically hides phone numbers, email addresses, links and social media handles in what users write (section 4). When a match ends, the conversation stays readable but no new messages can be sent.

### 2.4 Calendars and reminders

A guide can keep a calendar with their working hours, days off and bookings. A traveller booking that guide can only choose a time when the guide is free. The platform sends notifications in the app and by email about requests, bookings, changes, reminders before a trip and the outcome of a trip.

### 2.5 Account security

Signing in may require a code sent by email, always when we do not recognise the browser. You can see the browsers signed in to your account, sign any of them out, and sign out everywhere. We may email you about a new sign-in or a suspicious one, with a link to secure your account.

## 3. No responsibility for services or behaviour

To the fullest extent permitted by law:

- We are not responsible for the type, content, quality, safety, legality or timing of any service a guide offers or provides, or for whether it matches its description.
- We are not responsible for the behaviour, statements or actions of any user, on or off the platform, before, during or after a meeting.
- We check a user''s identity only where the profile shows them as verified. We do not check qualifications, licences, insurance or background. Profiles, ratings and reviews are written by users and reflect their own views.
- You use the platform and meet other users at your own risk. Take sensible precautions: meet in public places, tell someone where you are going, and never share bank or card details.

Nothing in these terms limits liability that cannot be limited by law, such as liability for death or personal injury caused by our negligence or for fraud, and nothing affects your statutory rights as a consumer.

## 4. Your obligations

Travellers and guides alike agree to:

- give accurate information, keep it up to date and use only their own account, with one account per person;
- treat other users with respect, and never harass, threaten, discriminate against, deceive or endanger anyone;
- obey the law, including any licence, permit, tax or insurance requirements that apply to the services they offer or use;
- use the platform only to arrange guiding services, and not post content that is false, offensive or infringes anyone else''s rights;
- keep contact and payment on the platform: not put phone numbers, email addresses, links or social media handles in profiles, reviews or messages, and not ask for or make payment for a booking outside BeLikeLocal;
- use the trip start, meetup confirmation, cancellation and review features honestly, and never confirm a meeting that did not happen.

Profile text that contains contact details is refused; in messages, reviews and booking notes they are hidden. Guides are solely responsible for the services they offer, their prices and honouring the bookings they accept.

## 5. Fees, bookings and cancellations

Prices for selection packs and guide fees are shown before you pay. The rules below, and the amounts shown in the app before each step, form part of these terms.

### 5.1 Protected by BeLikeLocal

Bookings made through BeLikeLocal (and paid here, where the guide charges a fee) are protected:

- Refunds by fixed rules (section 5.5): in full if you withdraw before the guide accepts, if the guide declines or doesn''t answer in time, if the guide cancels (plus 5% when they cancel late) or if the trip is never started; the fee minus 5% if you cancel before the start and the guide agrees.
- A fair process when something goes wrong after the start: the guide confirms your cancellation, or our team reviews the trip and decides the refund (section 5.7).
- Help with complaints: we can look at the booking, its meeting place, how the start was confirmed and your messages on the platform (section 6).
- Honest reviews: only people who actually finished a trip together can review each other.

Arrangements made outside the platform are not protected: if you pay a guide directly or move the conversation elsewhere, we cannot refund you or help with a dispute, and that trip does not count towards reviews, levels or your place in search results.

### 5.2 Selection packs and picks

A selection pack costs £5 and holds 5 picks, plus one for each traveller level, up to 10. Choosing "Interested" on a guide uses a pick; rejecting is free. A pick is returned if you withdraw your interest before the guide answers, or if a booking with that guide is cancelled. Picks do not expire. Packs are not refundable once a pick has been used. Some traveller levels unlock a few days of unlimited free picks (section 5.9).

### 5.3 Booking a guide

A guide who charges is booked by paying their fee in the app, for a meeting time (a free time in their calendar, if they keep one), an optional trip length and an optional meeting place. The request then waits for the guide:

- the guide accepts it, and it becomes a confirmed trip, or declines it;
- you can withdraw it while it waits;
- if the guide hasn''t answered a day before the meeting, we remind them; 15 minutes before the meeting both of you are warned; at the meeting time an unanswered request is cancelled.

A guide who guides for free has no fee: the trip is confirmed as soon as you match, and the two of you agree the time in the chat. Either side can set or change the meeting place, and the other is told. We remind both of you a day and two hours before a confirmed trip.

### 5.4 Starting a trip

The guide starts the trip in the app when you meet. The "Start the trip" button opens 15 minutes before the meeting time. While the trip is about to start and the app is open, both apps share the device''s location with us every 30 seconds, so the platform can confirm you are together: the button unlocks only when both locations put you within 50 metres of each other. If either location is missing, out of date or not precise enough, both of you are asked to confirm the meetup instead, and the button unlocks once both have. The traveller is told when the trip has started. Locations used for this are never shown to the other person (section 9.2).

### 5.5 Cancellations and refunds

- You withdraw a request before the guide accepts: full refund.
- The guide declines, or doesn''t answer by the meeting time: full refund.
- The guide cancels a confirmed trip: full refund, plus 5% of the fee, paid by the guide, when they cancel less than 24 hours before the meeting (or less than 2 hours before it if you matched less than a day earlier).
- You ask to cancel a confirmed trip before it starts: you give a reason; if the guide agrees you are refunded the fee minus a 5% cancellation fee, shown in the app before you ask; if the guide refuses, the booking stands.
- After the start: see section 5.7.
- Cancelling a trip ends the match on both sides and returns the traveller''s pick. A free trip can be cancelled at any time by unmatching.

### 5.6 Trips that never start

A confirmed trip that nobody started by the end of its time — the meeting time plus its length, or three hours if no length was given — is cancelled automatically and the traveller is refunded in full straight away. It moves to your past trips, and you stay matched, so you can book another date.

### 5.7 Cancelling after the start

If the guide has started the trip and you didn''t actually meet, or something else went wrong, you can cancel it in the app with a reason. There is no automatic refund: if the guide agrees, you are refunded in full; if the guide refuses, or doesn''t answer within 24 hours, the trip goes to our team as a dispute. We review the booking, how the start was confirmed and your messages, and decide the refund, from nothing to the full fee. Both of you are told the decision. A disputed trip cannot finish or be reviewed until it is decided.

### 5.8 Finishing a trip and reviews

A trip with a known length finishes automatically when that length has passed since its start; otherwise either side marks it finished and the other confirms. After a finished trip you can review each other once per trip with a grade from 1 to 5 and an optional comment of up to 256 characters, which you can edit or delete. Reviews are kept per role, and a profile''s rating comes only from them.

### 5.9 Levels, platform fees and bonuses

Each role has a level, from 0 (New) to 7 (Icon), earned only from paid, finished trips: one point per trip as a traveller, between one and one and a half per trip as a guide depending on the fee. Levels 1 to 7 need 1, 3, 6, 12, 24, 48 and 96 points. A guide who has only guided for free is shown as a Volunteer.

- Travellers get one more pick per pack for each level (up to 10), and at levels 2, 4 and 6 a bonus of 3, 7 or 14 days of unlimited free picks.
- Guides pay a platform fee on each paid booking, taken from the fee: 15% at levels 0 and 1, then 14%, 12%, 10%, 8%, 6% and 5% at level 7. It is fixed when the booking is paid and shown to the guide before they accept. Levels 4 and 6, and 10, 25 and 50 different reviewers averaging at least 4.8 stars, each give a bonus of fee-free days.

You start a bonus yourself from your profile. Our team may adjust a level or award a bonus or badge, and sanctions can lower a level and pause bonuses (section 6).

## 6. Complaints and sanctions

If you have a problem with another user, use the Report button on their profile or write to {{contact_email}}. One report about the same person can be open at a time. Every complaint is dealt with individually, on its own facts. We may ask both parties for their account of events and any evidence, and may read the messages between them on the platform. The person you report is not told who reported them; you are told when your report has been reviewed, but not what was decided about someone else''s account.

Depending on the outcome, we may take one or more of these measures:

- a warning;
- removing content;
- lowering your level, pausing your bonuses or lowering your place in search results, for a period or permanently;
- suspending (freezing) the account for a period or permanently: you cannot sign in, your profile is hidden, conversations with you become read-only and your open bookings are cancelled with a refund we decide, or left to run;
- permanently banning the person from the platform.

In serious cases we may act immediately and without notice, and report the matter to the authorities. A person who has been suspended or banned may not open a new account; we may refuse a new account from a browser used by a suspended one. To protect users we automatically note accounts that appear to belong to the same person (for example the same browser); our team reviews them and nothing happens automatically. We will tell you about a decision that affects your account and why, unless the law or the safety of others prevents it, and you can ask us to review it by replying to that message.

We decide disputes about a started trip as described in section 5.7. Otherwise we are not obliged to settle disputes between users, including about the quality of a service, but we will try to help where we reasonably can.

## 7. Closing your account

You can close your account at any time by writing to {{contact_email}}. We may suspend or close an account that breaches these terms, as described in section 6.

## 8. Changes to these terms

We may update these terms. If a change is significant, we will tell you in the app and ask you to accept the new version. The version date is shown at the top.

## 9. Privacy notice (GDPR)

### 9.1 Who is responsible for your data

- Data controller: {{controller_name}}, {{controller_address}}. Contact: {{controller_contact}}.
- Data protection officer: {{dpo_contact}}.
- Representative in the EU or UK, where required: {{representative}}.
- Data processors acting on our behalf: {{processors}}.

### 9.2 What we collect

- Account data: email address, password (stored only as a secure hash), roles, name, phone number and photo, and which version of these terms and the agreements you accepted.
- Profile data: date of birth, gender, headline and description for each role, languages, interests, working hours, prices, calendar, the area where you guide or are looking for a guide (rounded to about 1 km) and any other details you add. Food allergies count as health data: we process them only with your explicit consent, which you give by adding them, and you can remove them at any time.
- Activity data: your choices and matches, selection packs, bookings, payments and refunds, trip plans, reviews, levels, bonuses, reports and notifications.
- Messages and shared locations: what you write to the people you are matched with and any location you choose to share with them (contact details are hidden automatically); and a record that an attempt to share contact details was blocked or hidden (never its text).
- Trip start data: while a confirmed trip is about to start and the app is open, your device''s location and its accuracy, every 30 seconds, and whether you confirmed the meetup. It is used only to confirm that you and the other person are together, and to deal with a dispute about the trip.
- Security and device data: sign-in codes and links, the browsers signed in to your account, a sign-in history (successful and failed attempts, your IP address and the approximate place it suggests), and technical details your browser reports — browser and system, screen, time zone, languages, processor and memory class. We store those details as one-way codes and keep only a readable label such as "Chrome on macOS" for your own list. We do not use canvas or graphics fingerprinting.
- Server logs: requests and errors, without passwords, codes or links.

### 9.3 Why we use it and our legal basis

- To provide the platform under our contract with you (Art. 6(1)(b) GDPR): accounts, matching, chat, bookings, payments, starting and finishing trips, refunds, reviews, levels, notifications and emails about your account.
- Our legitimate interests (Art. 6(1)(f)): security, detecting suspicious sign-ins and linked accounts, preventing fraud and abuse, keeping contact details off the platform, ranking profiles, handling complaints and disputes, enforcing these terms and improving the service.
- Legal obligations (Art. 6(1)(c)): for example accounting records and requests from authorities.
- Your consent (Art. 6(1)(a) and Art. 9(2)(a)): optional sensitive details such as food allergies, and your device''s location, which your browser asks you for. You can withdraw consent at any time; without your location, trips start by confirming the meetup.

### 9.4 Who sees your data

Other users see your public profile for the role they are looking at: name, photo, age, headline, description, profile details, badges, level and reviews, and for guides the town where they guide. Guides see the town and dates of a traveller''s search area and upcoming trip stops. Your email address and phone number are never shown to other users. We share data with the processors listed above only as needed to run the platform — including email delivery, place search and, for the trip planner, an AI provider — and with authorities where the law requires it. We do not sell your personal data.

### 9.5 Transfers outside the EEA and UK

Where data is transferred outside the EEA or the UK, we rely on an adequacy decision or on the European Commission''s Standard Contractual Clauses. You can ask us for a copy of these safeguards.

### 9.6 How long we keep it

- Account, profile, bookings and reviews: while your account is open; after it is closed we delete or anonymise them within {{retention_period}}, unless the law requires us to keep them longer or we need them for an open complaint or dispute.
- Messages and shared locations: while both accounts in the conversation are open; deleted when either is deleted.
- Trip start locations: kept with the booking, for as long as the booking is kept.
- A traveller''s search area: used for 30 days and deleted when you clear it.
- Sign-in history: 12 months; IP addresses in it: 90 days. A sign-in lasts up to 30 days without use and at most 90 days.
- Server logs: 7 days. Email records: 30 days, and the text of an email is erased as soon as it is sent.
- Reports: as long as needed to deal with them and any follow-up.

### 9.7 Your rights

You have the right to access your data, correct it, have it erased, restrict its use, receive it in a portable format, object to processing based on our legitimate interests, and withdraw your consent. Write to {{controller_contact}}; we will reply within one month. You also have the right to complain to a supervisory authority: {{supervisory_authority}}, or the authority where you live.

### 9.8 Storage on your device

The app uses only what it needs to work, so it doesn''t ask for consent: two cookies that scripts cannot read — one that keeps you signed in (up to 90 days) and one that recognises your browser for security (400 days) — and a few items in your browser''s local storage: a summary of your signed-in account, your language and role, remembered-device tokens, choices not yet sent, your search place for the session, and whether you have seen this notice and the first-visit intro. We do not use advertising, analytics or tracking cookies.

### 9.9 Automated decisions and AI

Some things happen automatically, and none of them has a legal or similarly significant effect on you without a person being able to review it: the order of profiles (section 2.2), hiding contact details in what you write, checking whether you are together when a trip starts, cancelling and refunding requests and trips as described in section 5, and scoring how unusual a sign-in is, which may lead to an emailed code. Accounts that look linked are only flagged for our team.

The trip planner sends what you type about your trip, and the public profile text of guides near your stops, to an AI provider, which reads your itinerary and suggests guides with a short reason. It does not receive your contact details. Its suggestions are only suggestions; check them before you decide.

